# confronted — a witness who came for you blocks every act but the few that answer them
#
# A crime on the Test Roof fails within earshot of the hall, and the brewer comes up to look. He came
# because of you, so he confronts you: the exit is RUNAWAY, and a lawful act (contemplating him)
# is refused before any roll — the witness-side twin of an enemy in the room. Walking off to the next
# area used to end it for the price of one move.
#
# --doubt low: one try, no iterative thinking — a retry would step around the refusal
# this script is about (see thinking_iterates.cli and thinking_click_rules_not_retried.cli for the retries).
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --grant-mm brute_force --means-only brute_force --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Roof" --period noon --observe-only "goat" --doubt low

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180

regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect-outcome npc_drawn_in

# The phase carries on, and the brewer, come up to look, is observed in the live text. Now try
# something lawful.
click button
advance 12 180
expect RUNAWAY
goal contemplate
# The phase carried on, and whoever came in is observed in the live text below what was there —
# so their keyword is not keyword 0 (that is still the first thing observed), and is named instead.
click keyword man
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
regions
# The phase carried on past the first act (NarrativeController.ContinueNarrationSegment): its
# buttons are still on screen, spent, and keep their numbers, so the next act's button follows them.
click action 2
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect watching me
expect-no-outcome dialogue_trigger
quit
